{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Except the bread that he eats.</b> As it is written in the section of מקץ: ״כי לא יוכלון המצרים לאכול את העברים לחם כי תועבה היא למצרים״ — because they are coarse-spirited, as it is written regarding the Egyptians: ״לכן קראתי לזאת רהב הם שבת״, and therefore he did not appoint him over the bread. Another interpretation: Potiphar did not know about Joseph any disgraceful thing, except the bread that Joseph ate with him, and it is written: ״לא יוכלון המצרים״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:02.710670107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}